# Caddy in front of Agent Artifacts. Two sites, one for each host the app serves.
#
# The app signs people in itself (AUTH_MODE=password), so Caddy only does three things: it
# answers on both hostnames, it serves HTTPS for real domains (certificates are automatic), and it
# passes every request to the app. It asks for no login, adds no headers and keeps no list of paths.
#
# The addresses come from .env (APP_ORIGIN, CONTENT_ORIGIN). The defaults are for the local trial.
#
# Caddy passes the Host header on unchanged, which the app needs to tell the two sites apart.
# Caddy sets no limit on the size of a request body, so large publishes to /mcp go through.
#
# X-Forwarded-For: the app rate-limits sign-in attempts by the first entry. Caddy replaces a value
# the client sent with the real client address, unless the client is in `trusted_proxies`. This
# file does not set `trusted_proxies`. Leave it that way, unless another proxy (a CDN) sits in
# front of Caddy.

{$APP_ORIGIN:http://localhost:8080} {
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}

{$CONTENT_ORIGIN:http://content.localhost:8080} {
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
